# Auth0 API route auth

## Gebruik getSession(request), niet withApiAuthRequired

De `withApiAuthRequired` wrapper roept `getSession()` aan zonder request. Dat kan in sommige contexten (Next.js 15/16, modals) falen. Gebruik daarom expliciet `getSession(request)` en controleer de session zelf.

- **Niet doen**: `auth0.withApiAuthRequired(async (request) => { ... })`
- **Wel doen**: `export async function GET(request, { params })` met handmatige session-check

```javascript
// ❌ NIET
export const GET = auth0.withApiAuthRequired(async (request) => {
  const session = await auth0.getSession(request);
  const user = session.user.sub;
  // ...
});

// ✅ WEL
export async function GET(request, { params }) {
  const session = await auth0.getSession(request);
  if (!session) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
  }
  const user = session.user.sub;
  if (!user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "User not found" }, { status: 404 });
  }
  // ...
}
```

## Voor routes met dynamische params

Gebruik `context` voor params (bijv. `[id]`):

```javascript
export async function PATCH(request, context) {
  const session = await auth0.getSession(request);
  if (!session) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
  }
  const user = session.user.sub;
  if (!user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "User not found" }, { status: 404 });
  }
  const { id } = await context.params;
  // ...
}
```
